{"number":772,"title":"chrome-extension RULES.md isn&#39;t findable: 14 statement-of-the-world bullets, several rules per paragraph","body":"`packs/chrome-extension/RULES.md` is 14 bullets averaging ~70 words. Each opens with a fact about the platform (&#34;An MV3 service worker&#39;s relative paths resolve…&#34;, &#34;`host_permissions` does not bypass CORS&#34;) rather than with the act that brings a reader to it, and several carry more than one rule in a single paragraph (the three CDP traps; CORS-still-applies plus don&#39;t-list-your-own-backend; the runtime permission request plus the startup reconcile; the classic-loader pattern plus the `web_accessible_resources` graph).

Consequence: someone hitting a problem has to read the whole file to find the rule that applies. This is exactly the failure mode the `authoring-agent-docs` skill&#39;s &#34;Shape a rule so it fires&#34; section describes — a rule keyed to a state never fires, because nothing brings the reader to it — and the shape `packs/basics/RULES.md` already uses.

Re-key each rule to its trigger (bold situation first, one block per situation) and group the blocks under headings. No rule changes: nothing added, weakened, strengthened, or removed.","state":"open","html_url":"https://github.com/[REDACTED:env:CCR_TRIGGER_REPO]/issues/772","user":{"login":"missingbulb","id":73882448,"profile_url":"https://github.com/missingbulb","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73882448?v=4"},"author_association":"OWNER","reactions":{"total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"created_at":"2026-08-12T18:39:59Z","updated_at":"2026-08-12T18:39:59Z","has_parent":false,"has_children":false,"closed_by_pull_requests":{"total_count":1,"references":[{"number":773,"title":"chrome-extension pack: re-key RULES.md to situations so a reader can find their rule","state":"CLOSED","url":"https://github.com/[REDACTED:env:CCR_TRIGGER_REPO]/pull/773","repository":"[REDACTED:env:CCR_TRIGGER_REPO]"}]}}

{"number":722,"title":"Align the website repos&#39; release flows on one github-pages-serving standard","body":"EdFringeNow, ClaudiniteWebsite and MissingBulbWebsite each hand-roll the same GitHub Pages release flow with local drift (copied `bump-version.mjs`, deploy-on-every-push, analytics-token injection, no tags or releases). The canon `static-website` pack (#611) owns this territory but has zero adopters; MissingBulbWebsite&#39;s adoption attempt (its PR #39) is stalled on the disapproved #626.

Task: compare the three flows, analyze whether the consolidation policy/process is sound, and design the corrections — eliminating the bespoke mechanisms into a Claudinite pack, minimizing GitHub Actions surface (logic in the vendored engine where no secret/token forces Actions) and minimizing manual repo-settings changes, while keeping the flow customizable per repo. Acceptance probe: purge all release aspects and settings from MissingBulbWebsite so it simulates a fresh repo, adopt the pack, and the first release works on the first go.

Deliverables on this branch: `docs/website-release-flows/COMPARISON.md` and `DESIGN.md`.","state":"open","html_url":"https://github.com/[REDACTED:env:CCR_TRIGGER_REPO]/issues/722","user":{"login":"missingbulb","id":73882448,"profile_url":"https://github.com/missingbulb","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73882448?v=4"},"author_association":"OWNER","reactions":{"total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"created_at":"2026-08-09T10:16:02Z","updated_at":"2026-08-09T10:16:02Z","has_parent":false,"has_children":false,"closed_by_pull_requests":{"total_count":0,"references":[]}}

{"number":455,"title":"enable_pr_auto_merge is unusable on this repo — every merged-pr task falls back to manual merge","body":"Both `merged-pr`-ceiling tasks that ran a merge today failed to arm auto-merge, for what look like two different surfaced reasons, and both subagents fell back to a manual `merge_pull_request` call once required checks were green (self-reported deviation in both cases; verified independently — see issues #428 and #425&#39;s convergence comments for evidence checked against `pull_request_read`/check-run state).

- **growth-extract (PR #436):** `enable_pr_auto_merge` refused while `test-and-conformance` was still `in_progress` (&#34;unstable status&#34;), then refused again once it went green: *&#34;already in clean status (all checks passed) — auto-merge only applies when checks are pending.&#34;*
- **conversation-extract (PR #438, via a concurrently-dispatched run — see #452):** `enable_pr_auto_merge` first returned &#34;required checks are failing&#34; while the check was `in_progress`, then once green returned **&#34;Protected branch rules not configured for this branch.&#34;**

The second message suggests the root cause: GitHub&#39;s auto-merge feature requires the repo to have a branch protection rule (or the &#34;Allow auto-merge&#34; repository setting) configured on the target branch, and this repo apparently doesn&#39;t have one. If so, `enable_pr_auto_merge` will never succeed here regardless of check timing — every `merged-pr`-ceiling task (`growth-extract`, `growth-discover-packs`, `conversation-extract`) will keep hitting this and improvising a manual-merge fallback, which:

1. Isn&#39;t what the task docs literally instruct (&#34;arm auto-merge... never manually force-merge yourself&#34; was the executor&#39;s own dispatch instruction today, since the docs assume auto-merge works);
2. Works today only because each subagent independently chose to wait for green CI before merging — a good instinct, but it&#39;s ad hoc judgment standing in for a structural guarantee, and a future run (or model) could get that judgment wrong;
3. Trips the harness&#39;s generic &#34;self-authored PR merged without review evidence&#34; security flag on every single run, which is noisy and will desensitize whoever reviews these flags.

**Suggested fix (for owner/engineering, not doing this myself — outside an executor session&#39;s write surface):** enable &#34;Allow auto-merge&#34; in repo settings (Settings → General → Pull Requests) and/or configure a branch protection rule on `main` that auto-merge can attach to. Once that&#39;s in place, re-verify a `merged-pr` task can actually arm auto-merge end-to-end rather than needing the manual-merge workaround.","state":"open","html_url":"https://github.com/[REDACTED:env:CCR_TRIGGER_REPO]/issues/455","user":{"login":"missingbulb","id":73882448,"profile_url":"https://github.com/missingbulb","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73882448?v=4"},"author_association":"OWNER","labels":["blocked"],"comments":1,"reactions":{"total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"created_at":"2026-07-26T11:17:25Z","updated_at":"2026-08-07T05:30:49Z","has_parent":false,"has_children":false,"closed_by_pull_requests":{"total_count":0,"references":[]}}

{"number":335,"title":"The vendored-mount flip strands member-authored docs describing the legacy mount; phase 3 needs a reference sweep","body":"From a design review of `mount/DESIGN.md` (#315).

**Problem 1 — member docs.** The flip converts wiring, but nothing sweeps member *prose*. GoogleCalendarEventCreator&#39;s `CLAUDE.md`, `dev/procedures/github.md`, and `dev/procedures/technicalGotchas.md` document Method B extensively — the tarball sync, the git-proxy rationale (#364 there), and the stale-mount gotcha whose remedy is &#34;re-run `.claude/hooks/sync-claudinite.sh` by hand&#34;. The morning after the flip, all of it describes a mount that no longer exists, and the re-run-the-sync-hook advice is **actively wrong guidance an agent may follow**. Pair the flip (or a follow-up note) with a per-member doc-reconciliation pass — or at minimum extend the flip&#39;s member issue to enumerate the stale docs for an attended session to fix.

**Problem 2 — phase 3 blast radius.** The chrome-release-vendoring incident (retirement stranded inline tolerances, canon main red, reverted — fixed by PR-gating deletions in #313) taught: the probe&#39;s surface must be reviewed against the deletion&#39;s blast radius. Phase 3 deletes the canon sync hook, bootstrap&#39;s transition appendix, and the worker&#39;s legacy branch. Before that lands: sweep for *references* to the retired plumbing (member docs included; out-of-repo Setup scripts are covered by the flip&#39;s re-paste issue), and land the deletion through the `claudinite/retire-migrations` PR gate so canon CI proves reference-safety.","state":"open","html_url":"https://github.com/[REDACTED:env:CCR_TRIGGER_REPO]/issues/335","user":{"login":"missingbulb","id":73882448,"profile_url":"https://github.com/missingbulb","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73882448?v=4"},"author_association":"OWNER","labels":["blocked"],"comments":2,"reactions":{"total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"created_at":"2026-07-18T19:50:01Z","updated_at":"2026-08-07T05:30:42Z","has_parent":false,"has_children":false,"closed_by_pull_requests":{"total_count":0,"references":[]}}

{"number":336,"title":"Standardize the pilot-cohort field (`flip.repos`) for notes with an agentic component","body":"From a design review of `mount/DESIGN.md` (#315). Enhancement.

The flip record&#39;s `flip.repos` gate (&#34;names the only members the worker may convert; widening after a clean pilot night is a one-line edit&#34;) is the right rollout primitive for any note carrying an **agentic** component: mechanical ops are unit-testable before landing, but agentic instructions are not — one green canary night is the only pre-fleet evidence available, and notes v2 makes agentic notes routine rather than exceptional.

**Fix.** Promote it from a one-off of the flip record to a standard optional field on the note-record shape (e.g. `pilot: [&#39;owner/repo&#39;]` → `&#39;fleet&#39;`), with pilot-one-night-then-widen as the documented default lifecycle for agentic notes. Mechanical-only notes skip it.","state":"open","html_url":"https://github.com/[REDACTED:env:CCR_TRIGGER_REPO]/issues/336","user":{"login":"missingbulb","id":73882448,"profile_url":"https://github.com/missingbulb","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73882448?v=4"},"author_association":"OWNER","labels":["quick-win"],"comments":1,"reactions":{"total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"created_at":"2026-07-18T19:50:06Z","updated_at":"2026-07-31T05:22:59Z","has_parent":false,"has_children":false,"closed_by_pull_requests":{"total_count":0,"references":[]}}

